# Methodology

## Modeling Approach
The simulator uses a backward-facing modeling approach.

Instead of starting from subsystem power generation, the model starts from mission demand and calculates the required performance of upstream components.

## Mission-Level Analysis
The simulation represents the main flight phases:
- takeoff
- climb
- cruise
- descent
- landing

Each phase has distinct requirements in terms of altitude, speed, duration, and power demand.

## Subsystem Models
The framework includes mathematical models for:
- aircraft dynamics
- aerodynamic performance
- propeller behavior
- electric motor behavior
- fuel cell system behavior
- battery electrical behavior

## Fuel Cell System
The fuel cell system includes stack behavior and balance-of-plant losses.

## Battery System
The battery is represented using an equivalent-circuit approach to capture electrical response and state evolution.

## Energy Management
Power split logic is phase-based and allocates power between fuel cell and battery according to predefined strategies.

## Environmental Effects
The framework accounts for atmospheric effects such as:
- pressure
- temperature
- air density
